  "Question": "What is the value of \\[ \\begin{aligned} &1{,}000{,}000{,}000{,}000 \\\\ &\\quad {}- 777{,}777{,}777{,}777? \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(222{,}222{,}222{,}222\\)",
    "B": "\\(222{,}222{,}222{,}223\\)",
    "C": "\\(233{,}333{,}333{,}333\\)",
    "D": "\\(322{,}222{,}222{,}223\\)",
    "E": "\\(333{,}333{,}333{,}333\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The first number is one more than \\(999{,}999{,}999{,}999\\). Using that nearby number avoids borrowing across the zeros. Each aligned digit then gives \\(9-7=2\\), so\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&1{,}000{,}000{,}000{,}000\\\\\n&\\quad-777{,}777{,}777{,}777\\\\\n&=222{,}222{,}222{,}222+1\\\\\n&=222{,}222{,}222{,}223.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{222{,}222{,}222{,}223}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
